ocard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krocard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krocard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krocard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krocard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krocard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krocard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krocard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krocard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krocard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-11-10T11:57:54Z","updated_at":"2021-11-10T11:57:54Z","body":"> However, the good thing is that the contract of the new TrackSelectionOverride.Builder.setOverrideForType actually allows us to do this internally because the method promises to only select the provided override for its type. So we can simplify such use cases by automatically disabling all other selections for the same track type.\r\n\r\nYes this is what I had in mind when I introduced the API. It makes for a much simpler usage for the client to only have to set one override per type.\r\n\r\nThe cl adding the logic of disabling every over track of the same type is still pending as it complexify the logic significantly due to backward compatibility for legacy overrides.\r\n\r\nI did not realize that it would cause an actual issue in multi audio renders. Sorry about that @moneytoo.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/965061542/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"krocard","id":6862950,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4NjI5NTA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6862950?v=4","gravata